From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] use PAC3 brightness scale for M4 BZI6 backlight

# Reason: fresh M4-0215 evidence shows the BZI6 adapter sends Settings brightness at 1x because AUTO_BRIGHTNESS_TYPE3 disables the donor-specific 100x branch, while the pinned Exynos9810 PAC3 panel expects 100x. The pinned native HAL passes the extension value unchanged.
# Affected: the exact BZI6 legacy SehLights patch and its SHA-256 preimage guard. Main backlight now always uses PAC3 scale 100 within the M4/G965F/SDK37 scope; other lights, SurfaceControl, auto-brightness configuration, kernel and HAL are unchanged.
# Verify: reconstruct the pinned BZI6 smali preimage, replay the revised patch byte-for-byte, exercise wrong-scope/hash negatives, rebuild the existing fork, inspect compiled services.jar and final image, then check raw brightness at modest Settings values with off/wake behavior.
# Rollback: remove 0216 from the series/source lock, restore the prior 0003 patch and hash guard, and rebuild; package 0215 remains the rollback image until the replacement is verified.

